517:
(a) License required. It shall be unlawful for the owner, lessee, or operator of an event facility to allow any licensed event at the event facility without first obtaining a license. Licenses shall be issued on a per event basis.
(b) License application. All applications for a license must be provided to the police chief. The police chief shall issue a decision within five business days of the application being filed.
(c) Required information. All applications for licenses must include, at a minimum, the following information, and shall be signed by the applicant:
(1) Name and address of the applicant;
(2) Applicant's height, weight, age, sex, race, and social security number for background check purposes;
(3) Photocopy of driver's license or other official photo identification of the applicant;
(4) The nature of and expected attendance at the licensed event;
(6) The desired duration of the licensed event (maximum is six hours);
(7) The application shall contain a statement that the submission of the application shall be considered consent that a background check may be run by the police chief at his or her discretion on the applicant, and a statement that all information contained therein is true and correct; and
(8) If the licensed event is being promoted or sponsored by someone other than the owner of the event facility, then each promotor or sponsor shall provide the information set forth in subsections 22-202(c)(1)—(7) above.
(9) Any additional information the police chief may find reasonably necessary for a fair determination as to whether the licensed event will endanger public health, safety or welfare.
(d) License and identification carried. The signed license is to be kept on-site for the duration of the licensed event. Licenses shall be displayed at the request of any law enforcement personnel. Official photo identification shall also be kept on the person of the licensee at all times during the licensed event and shall be presented upon request of any law enforcement personnel. It shall be a violation of this article to fail or refuse to display a license or official photo identification when requested by law enforcement personnel.
(e) Cash bond. For each licensed event, the licensee shall be required to post a cash bond in the amount of $5,000.00, the purpose of which is to reimburse the city for any additional public safety or other costs occasioned by the event. Those portions of the bond not needed to reimburse the city for any additional public safety or other costs occasioned by the event shall be reimbursed to the licensee at the discretion of the city manager or his designee.
(Res. No. 04-2017, 2-17-17)
